WEBVTT

1
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.541
In verses 16.13 to 16.16,

2
00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:49.583
Lord Krishna described

3
00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:52.000
how demoniac people become entangled

4
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.791
in wealth, power, and indulgence.

5
00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:58.416
Now in verses 16.17 and 16.18

6
00:00:58.416 --> 00:01:00.041
He clarifies –

7
00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:02.791
this tendency does not remain only within.

8
00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:06.208
It shows itself in their religious conduct too.

9
00:01:06.208 --> 00:01:09.750
Here He exposes pretence, show, and even

10
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.000
envy toward

11
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.208
the Supreme.

12
00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:14.833
This is the turning point

13
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:16.083
where Lord Krishna

14
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.000
brings Himself into the picture directly,

15
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.291
and reveals that those of demoniac nature

16
00:01:22.291 --> 00:01:24.208
end up rejecting even Him.

17
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.958
In these verses Lord Krishna

18
00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:34.416
opens each part of the demoniac mind's

19
00:01:34.416 --> 00:01:37.208
structure one by one.

20
00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:40.291
First – atmasambhavitah,

21
00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:43.375
that is, self-worship.

22
00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:45.916
Making oneself the measure of all things,

23
00:01:45.916 --> 00:01:47.833
no external standard,

24
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:51.708
only one's own self-praise.

25
00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:56.583
Then – stabdhah, that is, rigid and arrogant.

26
00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:01.583
Not accepting the guidance of
scripture, saints, or well-wishers.

27
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:05.250
Then He says – dhanamana-madanvitah,

28
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.583
that is, the intoxication

29
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:10.833
of wealth, honour, and pride covers their vision.

30
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:14.375
Even religious practice becomes only superficial –

31
00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:16.666
‘Yajante namayajnaiste

32
00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:19.083
dambhena-avidhi-purvakam.’

33
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:22.500
That is, they perform rituals, but only in

34
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.958
name, filled with pretence,

35
00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:28.416
cut off from proper method and inner feeling.

36
00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:31.416
Thus dharma becomes not
personal transformation,

37
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:34.500
but public performance.

38
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.250
Clothing, charity, ritual – all may be present,

39
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.500
but the aim is not purification, only praise.

40
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.041
In verse 16.18,

41
00:02:44.041 --> 00:02:46.750
Lord Krishna places Himself in the picture –

42
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.916
‘Mam atma-para-

43
00:02:47.916 --> 00:02:51.791
deheshu pradvisanto abhyasuyakah.’

44
00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:56.208
This is not merely arrogance,
it is enmity toward God,

45
00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:58.708
toward the Paramatma dwelling in their

46
00:02:58.708 --> 00:03:02.500
own and in all other hearts.

47
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.125
And this enmity extends to His devotees –

48
00:03:06.125 --> 00:03:10.000
unjust criticism, dismissal of virtues.

49
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.541
Their refuge too is the opposite –

50
00:03:12.541 --> 00:03:16.666
ahankaram, balam, darpam, kamam,

51
00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:17.875
krodham.

52
00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:20.791
These qualities blind their vision.

53
00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:22.083
Instead of being humble,

54
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:25.500
they scorn the divine presence

55
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:30.291
and bind themselves ever deeper in bondage.

56
00:03:30.291 --> 00:03:33.583
Here Lord Krishna reveals the central

57
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:35.250
truth of the demoniac nature.

58
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.541
It is not merely delusion, but

59
00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:39.541
direct hostility toward

60
00:03:39.541 --> 00:03:41.125
the divine presence

61
00:03:41.125 --> 00:03:43.083
that exists within them.

62
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:50.750
I know –

63
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.583
you want to grow in life,

64
00:03:54.583 --> 00:03:56.291
spiritually

65
00:03:56.291 --> 00:04:00.291
and emotionally too.

66
00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:02.958
But The truth is –

67
00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:07.416
real growth does not happen

68
00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:08.791
when you keep

69
00:04:08.791 --> 00:04:12.583
admiring yourself in the mirror.

70
00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:15.375
The demoniac mind is

71
00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:18.916
atmasambhavitah –

72
00:04:18.916 --> 00:04:21.916
arrogant, rigid,

73
00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:24.041
and unwilling

74
00:04:24.041 --> 00:04:26.833
to listen.

75
00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.000
It feels –

76
00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.958
‘I already know enough.’

77
00:04:32.958 --> 00:04:35.333
This very pride

78
00:04:35.333 --> 00:04:38.250
becomes a wall.

79
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.500
Feedback may feel uncomfortable.

80
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.708
A comment may sting.

81
00:04:45.708 --> 00:04:48.458
But it is not an enemy –

82
00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:52.458
it is the door to transformation.

83
00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:56.416
If you surround yourself only with

84
00:04:56.416 --> 00:05:00.541
flatterers who praise you,

85
00:05:00.541 --> 00:05:05.875
and avoid those who challenge you,

86
00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:10.458
you will stay still.

87
00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:12.541
The appearance may change,

88
00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:17.291
but the mind will remain the same.

89
00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:20.500
Stop self-praise.

90
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.916
Where you avoid learning,

91
00:05:23.916 --> 00:05:27.916
ask yourself –

92
00:05:27.916 --> 00:05:31.125
‘Why am I stuck?’

93
00:05:31.125 --> 00:05:34.416
Instead of defending yourself from criticism,

94
00:05:34.416 --> 00:05:38.583
openly invite improvement.

95
00:05:38.583 --> 00:05:40.208
This is where

96
00:05:40.208 --> 00:05:44.041
real growth begins.

97
00:05:44.041 --> 00:05:48.291
The more you let go of pride,

98
00:05:48.291 --> 00:05:55.083
the more I fill you with clarity.

99
00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:59.958
Make humility your strength –

100
00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:04.750
and I will become your permanent guide.

101
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.083
Pride

102
00:06:11.083 --> 00:06:14.375
does not always roar.

103
00:06:14.375 --> 00:06:17.250
Often it whispers softly

104
00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.375
within the mind.

105
00:06:21.375 --> 00:06:24.375
‘I know everything.

106
00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:28.375
I do not need to listen to anyone.

107
00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:30.958
I am the one who is right.’

108
00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:35.958
Those who become darpa-madanvitah

109
00:06:35.958 --> 00:06:44.000
slowly begin to resent even Me.

110
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.541
‘Mam atma-para-deheshu pradvisantah’ –

111
00:06:47.541 --> 00:06:50.041
that is,

112
00:06:50.041 --> 00:06:51.750
Me who

113
00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.833
dwells within everyone.

114
00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:59.000
When ego

115
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.250
enters the home,

116
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:07.750
love quietly exits.

117
00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:12.333
Conversations become lectures,

118
00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:16.208
affection turns into competition,

119
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:20.708
and slowly bonds become hollow.

120
00:07:20.708 --> 00:07:23.458
Much noise,

121
00:07:23.458 --> 00:07:27.000
but no real connection.

122
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.041
Without even realising it,

123
00:07:31.041 --> 00:07:34.000
you stop hearing your partner's opinion,

124
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:41.458
your child's feelings, an elder's guidance.

125
00:07:41.458 --> 00:07:46.250
And then you are not only ignoring them –

126
00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:51.291
you are ignoring My voice too,

127
00:07:51.291 --> 00:07:53.291
because I

128
00:07:53.291 --> 00:07:57.000
speak through them.

129
00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:02.000
True family strength comes not from control,

130
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.958
but from humility.

131
00:08:04.958 --> 00:08:06.833
Learn to listen –

132
00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:09.375
not only words, but the language

133
00:08:09.375 --> 00:08:12.958
of the heart.

134
00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:14.625
Give every person's light

135
00:08:14.625 --> 00:08:17.625
the opportunity to shine,

136
00:08:17.625 --> 00:08:20.208
even if it is different

137
00:08:20.208 --> 00:08:23.375
from yours.

138
00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:27.083
When pride bows,

139
00:08:27.083 --> 00:08:30.125
love rises. And where

140
00:08:30.125 --> 00:08:34.333
love flows freely,

141
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:36.708
there divinity

142
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:38.000
takes root.

143
00:08:42.666 --> 00:08:44.750
If your work

144
00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:50.416
becomes a means to polish your own image –

145
00:08:50.416 --> 00:08:52.208
‘I am the best,

146
00:08:52.208 --> 00:08:56.500
I did it all, the stage is only mine’ –

147
00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.083
then understand,

148
00:08:59.083 --> 00:09:03.583
you have already stepped into
dangerous territory.

149
00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:06.208
I told Arjun –

150
00:09:06.208 --> 00:09:09.416
those who are atmasambhavitah

151
00:09:09.416 --> 00:09:13.666
and madanvitah,

152
00:09:13.666 --> 00:09:19.458
ultimately end up resenting even Me.

153
00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.166
Even when

154
00:09:21.166 --> 00:09:25.625
I speak through others –

155
00:09:25.625 --> 00:09:29.541
‘Mam atma-para-deheshu pradvisantah’ –

156
00:09:29.541 --> 00:09:32.500
even then, in the office

157
00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.458
this hostility does not show openly.

158
00:09:36.458 --> 00:09:41.333
It comes as silent rivalry.

159
00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:43.958
When someone else shines,

160
00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:46.750
you become uncomfortable,

161
00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.791
you question their ability,

162
00:09:49.791 --> 00:09:53.208
resist their ideas,

163
00:09:53.208 --> 00:09:56.375
and even begin to undervalue

164
00:09:56.375 --> 00:10:00.125
their achievements.

165
00:10:00.125 --> 00:10:02.041
Why?

166
00:10:02.041 --> 00:10:04.125
Because their growth

167
00:10:04.125 --> 00:10:08.250
challenges the image you have built

168
00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.416
of yourself in your mind.

169
00:10:12.416 --> 00:10:15.916
This is how a workplace atmosphere

170
00:10:15.916 --> 00:10:18.208
becomes toxic.

171
00:10:18.208 --> 00:10:22.208
Not from a lack of talent, but from pride,

172
00:10:22.208 --> 00:10:28.208
which turns collaboration into competition.

173
00:10:28.208 --> 00:10:33.375
If you truly want to lead, then

174
00:10:33.375 --> 00:10:35.125
give up the insistence that

175
00:10:35.125 --> 00:10:38.333
‘I am the most knowledgeable,
the sharpest, the most praised.’

176
00:10:38.333 --> 00:10:42.625
Let go of that insistence,

177
00:10:42.625 --> 00:10:45.958
and make space for others to grow.

178
00:10:45.958 --> 00:10:49.208
Where there is worth and talent,

179
00:10:49.208 --> 00:10:51.416
acknowledge it,

180
00:10:51.416 --> 00:10:54.916
even if it is not yours.

181
00:10:54.916 --> 00:10:57.041
Remember –

182
00:10:57.041 --> 00:11:00.041
respect for talent

183
00:11:00.041 --> 00:11:03.625
is what takes you to the heights of humility.

184
00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:07.583
And that very humility, in the truest sense,

185
00:11:07.583 --> 00:11:10.458
makes you worthy of respect.
